ly tastes like chicken because it’s made with it.</p><p>The first time I took a spoonful of this mix, stirred it right into my workday Maggi, and took a bite? Game changer. The noodle water transformed into a rich, savory base, and the whole dish finally felt complete.</p><p>But then, as I kept tweaking the formulation, a thought hit me.</p><h2>Why Limit It to Just Noodles?</h2><p>As the seasons start to shift—with the rainy monsoon season rolling in right now and the chilly winter months waiting just around the corner—our cravings naturally change. When it’s pouring outside or freezing in the office, you don’t always want a heavy plate of noodles or pasta. Sometimes, you just want a steaming, comforting mug of hot soup to hold in your hands.</p><p>So I engineered the powder to pull double duty.<img src="/img/soup01.png"
